{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 13, :comments ["<b>And his offering: one silver bowl.</b> Each one of them offered every kind of sacrifice — burnt offering and meal offering, sin offering and peace offering, and incense — to dedicate the altar and its service with every kind of sacrifice, except the guilt offering, for the sin offering and the guilt offering are one law for them. And Scripture recounts the offering of each one individually, to show that each one intended to atone for the particular sins that abounded in his tribe, and this through each part of his offering, to find favor before HaShem. And he leaned his hands and stood over them on behalf of his tribe, after the manner of the ma'amadot in public offerings."], :book :numbers, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 7, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:38:57.221062058Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}